
# Task 2: NumPy Arrays and Numerical Computation

## 1. Objective

The aim is to use NumPy arrays to store temperature readings and perform numerical calculations.

## 2. Inputs

The program uses 24 hourly temperature readings in degrees Celsius.

## 3. Mathematical Operations

The program calculates the mean, minimum and maximum temperatures. It also converts Celsius to Fahrenheit using:

F = 1.8C + 32

## 4. Original Output

The mean temperature is 23.12°C.

The minimum temperature is 17.5°C, while the maximum is 29.4°C.

The program also displays the first six Fahrenheit readings.

## 5. Modified Input

I changed the first temperature reading from 18.5°C to 20.5°C.

## 6. Observation

The mean temperature increased from 23.12°C to 23.20°C. The minimum and maximum temperatures remained unchanged.

## 7. Interpretation

Changing one temperature reading affected the average temperature but did not affect the minimum or maximum values.

## 8. Related Real-World Problem

A weather station can use NumPy to analyse daily temperature readings and monitor changes in weather conditions.

## 9. Assumptions

The weather station records 24 temperature readings per day. All readings are measured in degrees Celsius.

## 10. New Input Data

The first temperature reading was changed to 20.5°C. The other 23 readings remained unchanged.

## 11. Output

The modified mean temperature is 23.20°C. The minimum is 17.5°C and the maximum is 29.4°C.

## 12. Interpretation of the Modified Problem

The modified results show that NumPy can quickly calculate temperature statistics and update the results when new measurements are introduced.
